The ledger gate can become non-terminating or exhaust memory on a single corrupt ledger with a large sequence gap, which undermines the new CI/preflight check.

Review comment:

- [P2] Avoid materializing the full missing seq range — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-t1b/scripts/check-ledgers.sh:236-236
  When a ledger has a large accidental gap, e.g. seq `1` followed by `1000000000` with a matching sidecar, this builds a set containing every missing value before it can report the defect. That can hang or OOM the new CI/preflight gate instead of producing the intended bounded `BROKEN` output; compute only the first few missing values (up to `CAP`) without materializing the whole range.
